{"id":151226085657837,"type":"album","name":"Hellfire","artist":"black midi","year":2022,"weight":16,"info":{"cover":"https://cdn2.albumoftheyear.org/600x0/album/502843-hellfire_090504.jpg","aoty":82,"aoty_user":87,"yt":"Efmq_uXt1Rk","links":{"rateyourmusic":"https://rateyourmusic.com/release/album/black-midi/hellfire","aoty":"https://www.albumoftheyear.org/album/502843-black-midi-hellfire.php"},"desc":"\"Hellfire\" is the third and final studio album by English rock/post-punk band black midi, released on 15 July 2022 through Rough Trade Records. Produced by Marta Salogni, who had previously worked with the band in recording the song \"John L\" from their second studio album, the album was preceded by the singles \"Welcome to Hell\", \"Eat Men Eat\", and “Sugar/Tzu”. \"Hellfire\" was written while the band was isolating in London, with singer Geordie Greep calling \"Hellfire\" \"an epic action film if \"Cavalcade\" was a drama\". He described the characters depicted in the album as being \"scumbag. Almost everything I write ."},"artist_ref":{"id":86616365729783,"name":"black midi","info":{"img":null}},"labels":[],"genres":[{"id":138197775829889,"type":"genre","name":"Progressive Rock","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":439,"yt":null,"src":"rym"},{"id":55893123468232,"type":"genre","name":"Experimental Rock","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":373,"yt":null,"src":"rym"},{"id":191043281221162,"type":"genre","name":"Brutal Prog","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":366,"yt":null,"src":"rym"},{"id":3321080584815,"type":"genre","name":"Avant-Prog","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":214,"yt":null,"src":"rym"},{"id":229359158268774,"type":"genre","name":"Windmill Scene","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":109,"yt":null,"src":"rym"}],"lists":[{"id":52260166018782,"name":"RYM Top — Rock — Brutal Prog","src":"musthear","grp":"rateyourmusic","list_year":null,"rank":1,"year":null,"note":null,"total":200,"scaruffi":null},{"id":171836263770199,"name":"RYM Top — Scenes & Movements — W